<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Hardened-runtime entitlements for the notarized Cairn build.

    Deliberately minimal. Cairn is local-first (see docs/PRIVACY.md):
    the ONLY outbound network it makes is (a) fetching subscribed ICS
    calendar URLs and (b) the opt-in update check. macOS has no
    finer-grained outbound entitlement than network.client, so that one
    key covers both. There is no network.server entitlement — Cairn
    never listens on a network socket (its IPC is a Unix domain socket /
    named pipe, which needs no entitlement).

    NOT granted here, on purpose:
      - network.server: Cairn never accepts inbound network connections.
      - files.user-selected / downloads: CSV export uses the standard
        save panel, which is powerbox-mediated and needs no entitlement.
      - Accessibility: reading the frontmost window TITLE uses the
        Accessibility API, but that is a runtime TCC permission the user
        grants in System Settings - it is NOT an entitlement and signing
        is what lets the app appear in that list at all.

    If the WKWebView fails to load under hardened runtime on an older
    macOS, add `com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit` (true) - but verify it
    is actually required before weakening the runtime.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
